45	/// once and never again, so losing the startup race to snmpd - which is what
46	/// happens on a cold boot, where both start together - leaves the subagent
47	/// permanently disconnected with nothing logged anywhere. Measured on this
48	/// product: the framework connects on a manual restart and never on boot.
49	///
50	/// It also bounds how long after boot the session appears - which on this
51	/// product is every boot, not just an unlucky one.
52	///
53	/// The ping itself is synchronous (agentx_synch_response) and carries
54	/// net-snmp's own defaults of 1s timeout and 5 retries, so a ping to a master
55	/// that has gone away blocks this task for about 6 seconds before failing. At
